{
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "resolution_days",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A per-ticket duration is a strong axis for judging agent workload. However, the source samples show closed_at equal to sys_updated_on, so a resolution span requires opened_at (present in the table but not shown in samples). The produced values do not reconcile with the identical timestamps in the evidence, and negative values (-0.18, -0.15) are impossible durations, indicating some ungrounded/erroneous computation. Partial groundedness."
    },
    {
      "name": "workload_intensity",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.35,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Directly targets the query, so useful in principle. But it is an opaque composite score with no transparent derivation from the source text; values like 6.77 or 3.39 cannot be traced to specific evidence in the shown fields, and its heavy clustering on a few values plus apparent correlation with resolution_days suggests a partly invented/black-box construct rather than a grounded reading."
    },
    {
      "name": "critical_infrastructure",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A binary flag for whether the ticket touches critical infrastructure is a legitimate grouping axis for workload analysis. Many labels are defensible readings of short_description (database, VPN, intranet -> Yes; software update -> No). But the flag is asserted 'Yes' for 393/500 rows, including a generic 'Internet connection unstable', which stretches beyond what the terse descriptions clearly support, so groundedness is only moderate."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.83,
  "source_groundedness": 0.5,
  "rationale": "All three columns give genuine new axes (duration, an intensity score, and a criticality flag) aligned with the workload query, so analytical usefulness is solid. Groundedness is the weak point: resolution_days contains impossible negative values and does not reconcile with the identical timestamps shown; workload_intensity is an opaque composite with no traceable derivation; and critical_infrastructure over-asserts 'Yes'. Values often go beyond what the source text supports."
}

